hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24271","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, one of Banu Harithah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man cuts off the right of a Muslim man by his oath except Allah forbids Paradise to him and makes the Fire obligatory for him. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something small? He said: Even if it is a tooth-stick of arak."
"24272","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ja'far, narrated to us, al-Ala', meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed me, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b al-Sulami, from his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off the right of a Muslim person by his oath has made obligatory."
"24273","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed me, from al-Ala', from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off the right of a Muslim by his oath, Allah forbids Paradise to him and makes the Fire obligatory for him. He said: Even if it is something small? He said: Even if it is a stick of arak, saying it three times."
"24274","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, from Salih, meaning Ibn Kaysan, that Abdullah ibn Abi Umamah informed him, that Abu Umamah informed him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Plainness is part of faith, plainness is part of faith."
